WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:03.000
-You look great.
-Nice to be here.

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:04.133
-Welcome back.

00:00:04.133 --> 00:00:05.968
I wanted to apologize to you
straight up

00:00:05.968 --> 00:00:08.868
because I --
Crypto started to crash.

00:00:08.868 --> 00:00:10.000
-Uh-huh.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:11.200
-You know,
It's crashing now or whatever.

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:12.868
And I went up to you earlier
and I was like,

00:00:12.868 --> 00:00:14.000
"You must be bummed,"

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:15.934
because I thought
you told me about crypto."

00:00:15.934 --> 00:00:17.834
-No.
-It was not you.

00:00:17.834 --> 00:00:21.334
-No, but we've spent
the last five years being, like,

00:00:21.334 --> 00:00:23.000
sort of shamed about crypto.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:24.467
Like, "You got it?"
"No."

00:00:24.467 --> 00:00:26.400
"You're a coward?"
"No, yeah."

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:27.968
"You're stupid?
You're a stupid coward?

00:00:27.968 --> 00:00:29.434
You didn't get crypto?"

00:00:29.434 --> 00:00:33.734
And then it's been sort of
crashing the past couple months,

00:00:33.734 --> 00:00:37.367
and I got to say, it's been
pretty satisfying to watch.

00:00:37.367 --> 00:00:40.534
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yeah.

00:00:40.534 --> 00:00:42.567
Watching crypto crash is like

00:00:42.567 --> 00:00:46.467
watching the Fyre Festival
from a nearby boat.

00:00:51.167 --> 00:00:54.501
-People are reacting very
positively to your special,

00:00:54.501 --> 00:00:56.067
"Blocks," on Netflix.

00:00:56.067 --> 00:00:57.501
Congratulations.
-Thank you very much.

00:00:57.501 --> 00:01:01.234
-Do you...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:01.234 --> 00:01:03.000
Do you pay attention
to what people say

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:04.467
about you on social media?

00:01:04.467 --> 00:01:07.934
-Well, you've got to be careful
on social media, as we all know.

00:01:07.934 --> 00:01:11.767
For men, it's a lot of --
The social-media influencers

00:01:11.767 --> 00:01:14.501
for men are all --
I call them "the clappers,"

00:01:14.501 --> 00:01:16.334
because they start all their
posts like this --

00:01:16.334 --> 00:01:19.634
like, "What's up, guys?"

00:01:19.634 --> 00:01:21.767
If you're under 30,
I just have to let you know,

00:01:21.767 --> 00:01:25.868
no one's ever clapped
and said anything great.

00:01:25.868 --> 00:01:31.000
JFK wasn't like, "Ask not what
your country can do for you..."

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:33.100
-You're going on tour
next year, buddy.

00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:34.434
-Yeah.
-That's a big deal.

00:01:34.434 --> 00:01:35.567
-Thank you.

00:01:35.567 --> 00:01:36.834
-Do you have someone
watching the house?

00:01:36.834 --> 00:01:38.834
-I have someone -- My friend
Sarah watches the house.

00:01:38.834 --> 00:01:42.000
And she was watching it
this year when I was on tour.

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:48.434
And I have, like, a small pool,
and I had raccoons back there.

00:01:48.434 --> 00:01:51.834
And my first instinct was like,
"You got to, like, kill them."

00:01:51.834 --> 00:01:53.100
-Yeah, of course.

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:59.300
-And then she sent me video,
and they're so cute.

00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:01.634
I don't --
Can you show the video?

00:02:01.634 --> 00:02:04.000
-You brought the video of
raccoons in Neal's backyard.

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:05.601
Take a look at this.

00:02:05.601 --> 00:02:07.934
[ Audience "Awws" ]

00:02:07.934 --> 00:02:09.267
Oh, my gosh.

00:02:09.267 --> 00:02:13.000
They're just
cleaning themselves?

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:14.567
I mean, stop.

00:02:16.868 --> 00:02:19.334
-I think you got to
let them stay.

00:02:19.334 --> 00:02:20.434
-You've got to keep them.
-Right?

00:02:20.434 --> 00:02:21.868
-Yeah, you got to keep 'em.

00:02:21.868 --> 00:02:23.801
-And someone goes, "Are you
worried about getting rabies?"

00:02:23.801 --> 00:02:25.834
I was like, "They're not going
to give me rabies.

00:02:25.834 --> 00:02:28.567
They might give me wabies."

00:02:30.234 --> 00:02:32.267
-Wait. Because that's how
cute they are?

00:02:32.267 --> 00:02:35.601
-They're so cute,
they're going to give me wabies.

00:02:35.601 --> 00:02:38.167
And I'm going to have to
call 911 and be like,

00:02:38.167 --> 00:02:39.701
"I think I have wabies."

00:02:39.701 --> 00:02:43.267
They're like, "They're going to
send a wambulance over."

00:02:43.267 --> 00:02:44.767
And I'm going to go to
the hospital,

00:02:44.767 --> 00:02:46.601
and they're gonna go like,
"Do you have insuwance?"

00:02:46.601 --> 00:02:50.234
And I'm going to go, "I have
Bwue Cross and Bwue Shield."

00:02:50.234 --> 00:02:52.567
-That's how cute
those raccoons are.

00:02:52.567 --> 00:02:54.801
-They're that cute.
-They make you talk like a baby.

00:02:54.801 --> 00:02:57.501
You know, you talk
about dating in your stand-up.

00:02:57.501 --> 00:02:59.200
How's dating life going?

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:02.200
-If you have to ask,
it's not going great.

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:04.400
-That's true.

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:07.934
-Well, alright, the women I date
have always kind of, like --

00:03:07.934 --> 00:03:10.100
kind of bossed me around
a little bit.

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:13.701
I think they see me as,
like, a fixer-upper.

00:03:13.701 --> 00:03:15.934
Like I'm looking for a coach,
you know?

00:03:15.934 --> 00:03:19.067
So they would constantly be
telling me like --

00:03:19.067 --> 00:03:20.968
They'd always say like,
"I trained him.

00:03:20.968 --> 00:03:22.133
I taught him."

00:03:22.133 --> 00:03:23.834
Which is like --
You ever hear a guy say that?

00:03:23.834 --> 00:03:26.100
No, because you don't know
any pimps.

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:31.434
So, and then, like, women
would tell me what to do,

00:03:31.434 --> 00:03:35.467
and then you talked about this
on the show recently.

00:03:35.467 --> 00:03:39.501
I had a woman that I was dating.
We didn't even live together.

00:03:39.501 --> 00:03:43.834
She made me get rid of
a piece of art,

00:03:43.834 --> 00:03:45.968
and then no one believed me.

00:03:45.968 --> 00:03:48.901
And then you talked about it on
the show, and I'm so grateful.

00:03:48.901 --> 00:03:50.100
Please --

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:52.734
-I have a clip
of me talking about this here.

00:03:52.734 --> 00:03:54.501
-I love Buddy Holly
and I also love stained glass.

00:03:54.501 --> 00:03:55.634
-Okay.

00:03:55.634 --> 00:03:56.834
-And I don't know why
it just came up,

00:03:56.834 --> 00:03:58.200
and he's like,
"You love stained glass?"

00:03:58.200 --> 00:04:00.667
And he said something like,
"Do you like Buddy Holly?"

00:04:00.667 --> 00:04:02.033
I go, "I do, actually."

00:04:02.033 --> 00:04:06.100
He goes, "I have a stained-glass
portrait of Buddy Holly

00:04:06.100 --> 00:04:07.868
that my wife is like, 'There's
no way we're keeping this

00:04:07.868 --> 00:04:09.300
in the living room.'"

00:04:09.300 --> 00:04:12.901
So, I go, "I will borrow it,
and whenever you need it back,

00:04:12.901 --> 00:04:14.133
I will hang it in my office."

00:04:14.133 --> 00:04:15.501
And it's been in my office
since "Late Night."

00:04:15.501 --> 00:04:18.067
Neal Brennan,
if you need it back, I have it.

00:04:18.067 --> 00:04:19.267
That's you.

00:04:19.267 --> 00:04:21.367
Yeah, it was your girlfriend,
not your wife.

00:04:21.367 --> 00:04:23.534
-Yeah.
-But either way, I have it.

00:04:23.534 --> 00:04:27.067
It's been in my office, and...

00:04:27.067 --> 00:04:30.968
-I feel like,
if I could get it back...

00:04:30.968 --> 00:04:32.801
My girlfriend that
I'm dating now is here.

00:04:32.801 --> 00:04:35.133
Like, we could maybe --
We could bring it out?

00:04:35.133 --> 00:04:36.601
And we can...
[ Drumroll ]

00:04:36.601 --> 00:04:38.167
-Can we show it?
Can we bring it out?

00:04:38.167 --> 00:04:39.200
Come on over.

00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:41.200
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:50.767
This has been with me
for almost 15 years now.

00:04:50.767 --> 00:04:51.801
I can't believe that someone

00:04:51.801 --> 00:04:52.901
didn't want this
in their living room.

00:04:52.901 --> 00:04:54.067
-I know.

00:04:54.067 --> 00:04:56.467
And I feel like I'm in
a good place in my life.

00:04:56.467 --> 00:04:58.501
Isn't that cool?

00:04:58.501 --> 00:05:00.701
Like, I'm in a good place
in my life and I can --

00:05:00.701 --> 00:05:02.400
-You can tell by the silence
how cool it is.

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:04.367
-It's really --

00:05:04.367 --> 00:05:08.000
There's a reverent silence
for how cool this is.

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:09.367
So, I feel like
I'm in a good place --

00:05:09.367 --> 00:05:11.901
-Can I ask you this, though?
'Cause it has been mine.

00:05:11.901 --> 00:05:13.501
I don't want to lose it.

00:05:13.501 --> 00:05:15.033
I love it so much.
-Alright.

00:05:15.033 --> 00:05:16.133
-Where did you get it?

00:05:16.133 --> 00:05:20.133
-I got it in the street
in England.

00:05:20.133 --> 00:05:21.767
-That's even cooler.
I love it even more.

00:05:21.767 --> 00:05:22.901
-I know.

00:05:22.901 --> 00:05:24.467
-You got this on the street
in England,

00:05:24.467 --> 00:05:26.701
and now it's lived in
my office for 15 years.

00:05:26.701 --> 00:05:27.734
-Yeah.

00:05:27.734 --> 00:05:28.734
-And now I'm
giving it back to you.

00:05:28.734 --> 00:05:30.267
'cause I'm a man of my word.

00:05:30.267 --> 00:05:31.968
-Well, let me just --
My girl is here.

00:05:31.968 --> 00:05:33.467
And I feel like
we're in a good place

00:05:33.467 --> 00:05:36.501
and I can sort of
make my decisions.

00:05:36.501 --> 00:05:38.234
Val, will you stand up? Yeah.

00:05:38.234 --> 00:05:39.767
My girlfriend. Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:49.334 --> 00:05:52.167
So, babe, what do you think?
Can we keep it?

00:05:52.167 --> 00:05:53.734
-No, it's gross.

00:05:53.734 --> 00:05:56.834
-Yes! Exactly. Yes!

00:05:56.834 --> 00:05:59.968
It's mine again! Thank you!

00:05:59.968 --> 00:06:02.000
She's a keeper.
I love her, by the way.

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:03.534
Neal Brennan, everybody!

00:06:03.534 --> 00:06:06.167
His special,
"Neal Brennan: Blocks,"

00:06:06.167 --> 00:06:08.167
is streaming now on Netflix.

00:06:08.167 --> 00:06:10.534
We'll be right back with
a performance from Wizkid.

00:06:10.534 --> 00:06:11.634
Stick around.

